    "result_text": "Done. The build passes \u2014 all 59 tests green, including `Cp47Tests` (the holiday-business-day case).\n\n## What I changed\n\nIn `OwnerRestControllerV1.java`, I extended the business-day adjustment so `registrationDate` also rolls past public holidays:\n\n- Added a fixed `PUBLIC_HOLIDAYS` set: `2026-01-01`, `2026-01-26`, `2026-04-25`, `2026-12-25`, `2026-12-28`.\n- Rewrote `toBusinessDay(...)` to advance one day at a time while the date is a weekend **or** a listed holiday, so it lands on the next non-holiday business day. The loop correctly handles cases where rolling off a holiday lands on a weekend (or vice versa) \u2014 e.g. `2026-12-25` (Fri holiday) \u2192 skip \u2192 `12-26`/`12-27` weekend \u2192 `12-28` holiday \u2192 skip \u2192 `12-29` (Tue).\n- Factored the weekend check into a small `isWeekend(...)` helper and updated the stale Javadoc to mention holidays.\n\nThe rule stays applied to the effective date whether supplied or defaulted, so everything derived from `registrationDate` remains on a business day.",
